<title>USA: PS New Mexico delays San Juan unit restart.</title>
<headline>PS New Mexico delays San Juan unit restart.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 350 megawatt (MW) unit 2 at the San Juan coal-fired power plant in New Mexico will not be restarted until Thursday due to problems with a condenser, sources familiar with the plant's operations said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The unit, shut Friday night for tube leak repairs, had been expected to restart Tuesday.</p>
<p>San Juan's other 361 MW and two 540 MW units are said to operating at normal rates.</p>
<p>The power plant is operated by Public Service Co of New Mexico.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau 213-955-6761</p>
